                        "name": "Adrian Ambro\u017cewicz",
                        "email": "adrian.ambrozewicz@linux.intel.com",
                        "username": "aambroze"
                    },
                    "message": "As I look at the code, the function name is not very accurate.\n\nIt could be named `formatMessageOnError` and returned value could be `true` if there was an error and `false` if not, therefore further handling is required.\n\nCode would then read like so:\n\n```cpp\nif(!formatMessageOnError(asyncResp->res, args.id, ec))\n{\n  messages::created(asyncResp->res);\n  return;\n}\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/metric_report_definition.hpp",
                    "line": 772,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Michal Orzel",
                        "email": "michalx.orzel@intel.com",
